5915	
5916	### `pipeline/search.rs`
5917	
5918	Owns the 8-stage search pipeline plus scope filtering, language filter validation, and the rayon parallel block extraction. Key flow:
5919	
5920	1. Parse query (or escape-as-literal in `exact` mode); return empty with diagnostic if parsing yields zero terms.
5921	2. Build `QueryPlan` from `terms`; partition `lang_filters` into supported (`ts/tsx/js/jsx/mjs/cjs/mts/cts/rs/rust`) and unsupported; collect search patterns; bail with diagnostic when no positive patterns.
5922	3. Canonicalize workspace root, build the per-workspace session, derive `requested_languages` from CLI flag + lang filters, enumerate source files via `session.source_files`, filter by `path_filters` and `matches_lang_filter`.
5923	4. Emit `Skipped` diagnostic for unsupported requested languages; if `has_block_capability` is false for the requested set, return empty with diagnostic.
5924	5. Apply git scope: if `ImpactedNeighbors`, fetch `session.standard_index()` and call `git_scope::scope_files_with_index(files, &root, &opts.scope, Some(index.as_ref()))`; otherwise `git_scope::scope_files`. Surface scope diagnostics describing match counts.
5925	6. Compile term regexes honoring `case_sensitive`; build `scan_patterns` = positive patterns ∪ excluded term patterns.
5926	7. `text_search::search_files(&files, &scan_patterns, opts.limits.max_candidates, opts.case_sensitive)` gives `Vec<(path, Vec<LineHit>)>`.
5927	8. Parallel `into_par_iter` over hits: resolve analyzer per file, skip files whose analyzer lacks `capabilities().blocks`, apply boolean exclusion/required-term filtering, call `analyzer.analyze`, annotate blocks with `matched_lines`/`matched_keywords` restricted to lines that pass `git_scope::line_matches_line_scope`, tokenize each block via `rank::tokenize_block`.
5928	9. Aggregate per-language "block-extraction omitted" counts into a single diagnostic per language.
5929	10. Build `df` over tokens, rank via `rank::rank_blocks(all_blocks, &bm25_query_terms, &df)`, dedup via `dedup::dedup_blocks`, apply budget via `budget::apply_budget`.
5930	
5931	### `pipeline/symbols.rs`
5932	
5933	Modular workflow:
5934	
5935	- `run(files, lite)` — derives the workspace root from `files[0].parent()` and calls `run_with_options`.
5936	- `run_with_options(files, opts, lite)` → `run_with_options_scoped(files, opts, lite, None)`.
5937	- `run_with_options_scoped(files, opts, lite, scope)`:
5938	  - Drops `lite` (kept for API back-compat).
5939	  - Opens `WorkspaceSession`.
5940	  - If `scope.mode == FullRepo`, uses the caller-provided file list; otherwise calls `session.source_files(...)` with `allow_tests: true, no_gitignore: false, languages: None` to give the scope layer the broadest candidate set.
5941	  - Calls `apply_scope(&candidate_files, opts, &session, &scope, &mut diagnostics)` which itself calls `scoped_files` (which dispatches to `git_scope::scope_files_with_index` or `git_scope::scope_files`). Empty selection → return empty result with a "matched no supported files" diagnostic.
5942	  - Surfaces a `scope_diagnostic_message` describing changed file/line/hunk counts when applicable.
5943	  - `analyze_symbol_files` parallelizes per-file analysis (`AnalysisProfile::Structural`). Each outcome carries `symbols`, `classified` (only when `analyzer.capabilities().classified_imports`), `omitted_classified_imports`, and degraded diagnostics from `had_parse_errors`.
5944	  - For `ChangedLines` scope: symbols are filtered by `git_scope::line_matches_line_scope(selection, file, symbol.line)`.
5945	  - Per-file cap = 50, total cap = 500 — when total is hit, the in-progress file is truncated and `truncation_marker` is set, loop breaks.
5946	  - At the end, emits an aggregated `Warning` diagnostic if any files had `omitted_classified_imports` (Rust files trigger this; ChangedLines scope also increments it because import classification is file-level).
5947	
5948	### `pipeline/deps.rs`
5949	
5950	Owns `deps`, `deps_from`, `classify`, `migration_surface`, plus the shared `source_files` / `candidate_source_files` helpers. Defaults for migration:
5951	
5952	```rust
5953	const DEFAULT_LEGACY_PREFIXES: &[&str] = &["@viagogo/core", "styled-components"];
5954	const DEFAULT_TARGET_PREFIXES: &[&str] = &[
5955	    "@stubhub/broadway",
5956	    "@stubhub/broadway-foundation",
5957	    "@stubhub/broadway-web",
5958	    "@stubhub/broadway-ui",
5959	];
5960	```
5961	
5962	`deps` runs inspect via `inspect_with_options` then projects each `InspectEntry` through `dependency_summary` (which converts `ClassifiedImports` to `FileDependencySummary` for TS entries and `RustImports` for Rust entries).
5963	
5964	`deps_from` parallelizes per-file analysis with `AnalysisProfile::Dependencies` and filters `dep.target` matches via `dependency_target_matches` (handles `File`/`RustPath`/`Namespace` targets) and `package_matches` (exact match or prefix followed by `/`, `::`, or `.`). Builds `DepsFromEntry` lists with binding names from `dependency_binding_names` (formats `imported as local`, `*`, or just the local/imported name).
5965	
5966	`classify` runs per-file `dependency_specifiers_for_file` (also `AnalysisProfile::Dependencies`), then matches specifiers against the legacy/target prefix sets. Unsupported files produce `ClassificationEntry { status: "unsupported", score: 0.0, … }`.
5967	
5968	`migration_surface` is `classify` plus aggregation into `MigrationSurfaceSummary` with `adoption_pct = (target_files + mixed_files) / total`.
5969	
5970	`unsupported_file_message` formats: `"no analyzer registered for {language} files in this build"` using `source_scan::candidate_language(file)` to identify the language.
5971	
5972	### `pipeline/graph.rs`
5973	
5974	Owns `dependents` and `dependents_scoped`. Build flow:
5975	
5976	1. Canonicalize file and root; verify `abs_file.starts_with(abs_root)` else `PathOutsideRoot`.
5977	2. Open session; build `standard_index`.
5978	3. Look up the analyzer for `abs_file`. If no analyzer matches → `add_missing_analyzer_diagnostic("dependents", …)`, return empty.
5979	4. Call `require_precision_capability` on `resolved_import_graph` with `PrecisionRequirement { operation: "dependents", minimum: CapabilityPrecision::Structural }`. Below-structural surfaces "is not supported" and returns empty; structural-but-not-exact emits a precision-warning diagnostic.
5980	5. TypeScript-only: warn when no `tsconfig.json` is present at or above the workspace root.
5981	6. Fetch raw dependents/imports from `index.import_graph`.
5982	7. If scope is git-backed, narrow the result lists by `git_scope::scope_files_with_index(index.files.clone(), &abs_root, &scope, Some(index.as_ref()))`. For `ChangedLines`, attach a warning that "scope changed-lines falls back to changed-file behavior for dependents because the import graph is file-level."
5983	8. Cap each list at 200, set `truncation_marker` when either was capped.
