  "reasoning": "Methodology: re-read every cited source location directly rather than trusting the blocker report's line numbers or the prior draft's claims. Confirmed via Read: 01-core-architecture.md §3 (190-251, enum verbatim + post-research-correction note), miette feature wiring (83-87), io-errors FileIoError (2950-3018), persist.rs §16 in full (1499-1700, including CACHE_VERSION=2 at 1513, init at 1567-1584, load_cache at 1586-1607, flush at 1652-1680, evict_lru at 1682-1699), output.rs + main.rs (2400-2523, confirming render_error is dead code and Subcmd has exactly 5 variants, no init). Confirmed via Read: 03-multi-language-platform.md's git_scope.rs (1360-1564, validate_git_ref's 3 reason strings, effective_pr_range's 'merge-base' literal, collect_changes's 3 elided map_err sites at 1428/1430/1470, blob_at_ref/blob_at_ref_in_repo's 'show' literal and bare-String boundary), projection.rs (1570-1650, discovering the to_value Json sites at 1594/1602 that neither the prior draft nor the blocker report's citation list mentioned), io_safety.rs (2090-2131), WorkspaceIndex::build (2180-2258, confirming init() always precedes flush() in the only shown call chain) and pipeline/session.rs's for_workspace/standard_index (1225-1294, confirming the second LockPoisoned context string and that for_workspace also calls init() before any flush). Confirmed via Read: 02-inspection-and-analysis.md:1845-1897 (the run_ok_json test helper, confirming its serde_json::from_str call never touches MonoklError). Confirmed via Read: 07-edge-cases-and-failure-modes.md Part 1 in full (1-62), locating finding #5 at line 37 and finding #19 at line 54 exactly. Confirmed via Read: .claude/semantic-model/error-taxonomy.md in full, finding its own line ~60 'only caller'/'never returned to a caller' claim (matches the blocker's description) and its two 'Known contract gaps' entries (gap 1 = corruption/staleness, gap 2 = StaleDiskCache message) which I cited by exact line range instead of the dead research-report@1 pointer. Ran two targeted greps across docs/spec/*.md: one for 'serde_json' (surfaced the projection.rs sites, confirming the true Json call-site count is 8, at the top of the blocker's stated 6-8 disagreement range) and one for 'MonoklError::Git|MonoklError::Json|StaleDiskCache|::Io(FileIoError' (cross-checked every construction site I cite). Ran a corpus-wide grep for '#[diagnostic' across docs/spec/*.md and .claude/, confirming zero hits, grounding AC-002B. Key judgment calls, each marked judgment_call:true with rationale: (a) resolving Json cache-load to self-heal rather than hard-fail (AC-021), a genuine policy decision with no single 'correct' answer dictated by the source, justified by the corpus's own stated self-healing/decoupled-cache tenets; (b) choosing to document rather than silently patch flush()'s uncaught fallback (AC-013B), since patching would mean rewriting a verbatim code block in a document (01-core-architecture.md) outside SPEC-001's stated editing scope; (c) scoping AC-015 to the two spelled-out Git operation-tag sites rather than inventing the three elided ones, since inventing them would fabricate facts the source doesn't state; (d) reconstructing AC-023 without its original verbatim text, flagged explicitly so a reviewer checks it against whatever the true original said."
