    "Implementing or correcting docs/spec/04-analysis-fidelity.md's rust_visibility(node) or extract_impl_symbols functions themselves (04-analysis-fidelity.md:42-103) -- that is the Rust-fidelity-fix track's job. This track only locks the canonical types those functions must eventually conform to, and states that their current impl_owner/Visibility::Super output would not compile against those types.",
    "The Part 4 finding #3 signature-normalization discrepancy (07-edge-cases-and-failure-modes.md:140) -- whether SymbolEntry.signature should be produced by first_line_signature (truncate at the first newline, the existing behavior per 02-inspection-and-analysis.md) or 04-analysis-fidelity.md's proposed normalize_signature (whitespace-collapse across the full multi-line span). This spec locks that signature is Option<String>, present unconditionally as a JSON key (AC-005); it does not resolve which function populates its content.",
    "kind_detail's full value vocabulary -- only its type (Option<String>) and field presence/serde attributes are locked here (AC-004, AC-005). The set of valid kebab-case strings (e.g. \"rust-struct\", \"rust-impl\") is owned by each language analyzer's own track, per 03-multi-language-platform.md:2783 and 04-analysis-fidelity.md:81-88's own (as-yet-unlocked) table of values.",
    "owner's and trait_impl's population semantics -- which impl block or free-standing item produces which value, and the self-type-propagation rule from an impl block down to its associated fns -- are owned by the language-analyzer implementation track that constructs SymbolEntry values (e.g. the Rust-fidelity-fix track), not this type-shape track. Likewise, which language construct a given analyzer maps to SymbolKind::Other is an analyzer-level decision, not locked here beyond Other's existence as a valid variant (AC-001).",
    "Editing docs/spec/04-analysis-fidelity.md's own prose to replace impl_owner with owner and Visibility::Super with Visibility::Module -- that is a docs-consistency edit to a different file, outside a Rust-type-shape track's scope. This spec states the contradiction and its resolution (AC-007, AC-008) so that any future implementation of 04-analysis-fidelity.md must conform to the canonical types locked here; it does not itself patch that file's text."
  ],
