      "suggested_fix": "Add `AC-015` to T-017's covers_criteria (its green step already checks the 3/2 counts and that both feature keys exist in [features]), and strengthen T-017 to assert the module NAMES, not just counts: `diff <(grep -A1 'cfg(feature = \"lang-ts\")' /Users/gabe/Projects/monokl/crates/monokl/src/lib.rs | grep '^pub mod') <(printf 'pub mod enrich;\\npub mod indices;\\npub mod pipeline;\\n')` and `diff <(grep -A1 'cfg(feature = \"cli\")' .../lib.rs | grep '^pub mod') <(printf 'pub mod cli;\\npub mod output;\\n')`, plus the source cross-check `grep -c '^Modules gated on .lang-ts.: .enrich., .indices., .pipeline.\\. Modules gated on .cli.: .cli., .output.\\. Everything else is always compiled\\.$' /Users/gabe/Projects/monokl/docs/spec/01-core-architecture.md` expecting `1` (all three verified working). Narrow T-018's title, commit_message, and files.test to the unexpected_cfgs consequence only, and drop crates/monokl/src/lib.rs and crates/monokl/Cargo.toml from its files.test since no step reads them."
    },
    {
      "task_id": "T-020",
      "type": "under-specified",
      "description": "The real-manifest assertion added by fix #5 has no working-directory anchor. It runs `out_real=$( (cargo metadata --no-deps --format-version 1) 2>&1)` with no `cd`, no `--manifest-path`, and no absolute path -- the only cwd-dependent command in a plan that wraps every other cargo invocation as `(cd <abs-dir> && cargo ...)` specifically so the implementer's shell working directory is never load-bearing. If the shell is anywhere outside the monokl workspace, cargo either fails with a 'could not find Cargo.toml' error (rc 101 but no registry text, so REAL_REGISTRY_ERR does not print while REAL_EXIT_101 does -- a confusing half-pass) or resolves against an unrelated enclosing workspace and exits 0, so neither marker prints and the implementer sees silence rather than a clear failure. Note the assertion itself is correct: I verified against the real T-011 file state that cargo emits `registry index was not found in any configuration: \\`orin-cargo\\`` at rc 101, and that the fixed `.`-as-backtick grep pattern matches it.",
